1
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:44,000
Ketil's Farm

2
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:43,120
Einar, Thorfinn... Starting today,
you two are friends.

3
00:01:47,630 --> 00:01:49,480
Go on, say hello.

4
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:52,110
I'll be assigning the
two of you the same job.

5
00:01:52,110 --> 00:01:53,760
You're to work together.

6
00:01:55,170 --> 00:01:57,010
Nice to meet you, Thorfinn.

7
00:01:58,080 --> 00:01:58,900
Hello.

8
00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:03,460
Good. Let me explain what you'll be doing.

9
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:07,850
Einar, what does this place look like to you?

10
00:02:07,850 --> 00:02:10,070
What? Uh...

11
00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:13,290
A forest?

12
00:02:13,890 --> 00:02:15,880
Wrong.

13
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:21,080
This is a future wheat farm.

14
00:02:22,830 --> 00:02:25,790
I own these woods.

15
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:28,200
I'm going to let the two of you borrow them.

16
00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:29,960
Borrow?

17
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:33,050
Yes. I'll leave everything up to you.

18
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:37,070
You'll clear this land, work it,
and reap the harvest.

19
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:39,720
I'll buy it from you for a fair price.

20
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:45,600
Once that amount exceeds your price,
you'll buy yourselves back.

21
00:02:48,010 --> 00:02:49,710
Buy ourselves?

22
00:02:49,710 --> 00:02:53,900
In other words, we'll... we'll be free?

23
00:02:54,170 --> 00:02:59,660
That's right. Earn your freedom
yourselves, the right way.

24
00:03:00,310 --> 00:03:05,510
Depending on how hard you work, you may be
able to accomplish that within three years.

25
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:09,330
I'll wait to collect your lease payment
until after your first harvest.

26
00:03:11,330 --> 00:03:14,090
What's the matter? Is there a problem?

27
00:03:15,990 --> 00:03:19,550
N-No. Thank you. I'll do my best.

28
00:03:21,250 --> 00:03:22,310
Good.

29
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:27,390
If you have any problems
or questions, ask Pater here.

30
00:03:27,390 --> 00:03:29,940
He knows this farm well.

31
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:31,710
Nice to meet you.

32
00:03:31,710 --> 00:03:35,160
I became a free man by the same means.

33
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:38,450
I know it'll be tough working in an
unfamiliar land, but do your best.

34
00:03:38,450 --> 00:03:39,990
I w-will!

35
00:03:41,210 --> 00:03:44,450
For today, observe Thorfinn's work.

36
00:03:44,890 --> 00:03:47,270
You must be exhausted from the long journey.

37
00:03:49,830 --> 00:03:54,650
Thorfinn, be good to Einar. Got it?

38
00:03:54,650 --> 00:03:55,530
Yes, sir.

39
00:04:03,390 --> 00:04:05,420
Hey, our master...

40
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:06,230
Huh?

41
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:10,580
Hey, wait up.

42
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:15,480
What kind of man is our master?

43
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:22,600
Is this normal in Denmark?

44
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:28,470
We had slaves back in my homeland,
but they were slaves for life.

45
00:04:32,990 --> 00:04:37,320
I'm from Northern England. What about you?

46
00:04:40,770 --> 00:04:42,040
Iceland.

47
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:45,600
Iceland, huh?

48
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:48,460
Iceland...

49
00:04:49,830 --> 00:04:50,730
Where's that?

50
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:56,690
Wow, you've already cut down a ton of trees.

51
00:04:57,240 --> 00:04:58,690
How much is left?

52
00:05:01,590 --> 00:05:03,350
Everything on this side.

53
00:05:03,890 --> 00:05:05,110
This side?

54
00:05:08,230 --> 00:05:10,160
See that river over there?

55
00:05:10,490 --> 00:05:12,850
Everything on this side of the river.

56
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:17,620
This side of the river?

57
00:05:20,470 --> 00:05:22,100
You mean...

58
00:05:24,350 --> 00:05:27,560
There's still a lot left to clear?

59
00:05:46,070 --> 00:05:47,610
Huh? What?

60
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:49,370
Hup!

61
00:05:53,930 --> 00:05:54,470
Huh?

62
00:05:57,520 --> 00:05:58,980
What do you want?

63
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:02,130
He told you to observe.

64
00:06:03,270 --> 00:06:06,170
I want to free myself as soon as possible.

65
00:06:06,170 --> 00:06:07,390
What's wrong with that?

66
00:06:09,310 --> 00:06:12,660
In that case, could you
work a little farther away?

67
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:16,650
And cut them so they fall
perpendicular to the river.

68
00:06:17,630 --> 00:06:21,210
I see. So we float them down the river, huh?

69
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,490
Ow...

70
00:06:29,230 --> 00:06:31,740
Man, I'm hungry.

71
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:34,540
Hey, how does lunch work around here?

72
00:06:36,510 --> 00:06:37,590
We get lunch.

73
00:06:39,710 --> 00:06:43,800
That's good. Do we go pick it up somewhere?

74
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:46,940
No, the retainers should be bringing it soon.

75
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:50,810
Really? This place leaves
nothing to be desired.

76
00:06:52,030 --> 00:06:53,680
No way. Seriously?

77
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:54,940
Seriously.

78
00:06:54,940 --> 00:06:57,810
Hey, lunch is here. Right, Thorfinn?

79
00:07:01,570 --> 00:07:03,340
I'm telling you, seriously.

80
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:05,070
You're the only one who hasn't.

81
00:07:05,370 --> 00:07:07,570
Man, I had no idea.

82
00:07:07,570 --> 00:07:09,950
I guess I'll go see her tonight.

83
00:07:09,950 --> 00:07:11,670
Yeah, you should.

84
00:07:11,670 --> 00:07:13,150
Go and get rejected.

85
00:07:13,150 --> 00:07:14,460
That's not gonna happen.

86
00:07:16,170 --> 00:07:18,710
Hey, that must be the newbie.

87
00:07:18,710 --> 00:07:21,000
Yeah, looks like it.

88
00:07:21,670 --> 00:07:22,840
Look at that stupid face.

89
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,550
The face of a slave.

90
00:07:24,860 --> 00:07:26,600
H-Hello, I...

91
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:29,320
Yeah, we know. We've heard.

92
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:30,810
Um...

93
00:07:33,070 --> 00:07:35,070
What is this?

94
00:07:35,070 --> 00:07:37,320
Your lunch.

95
00:07:40,730 --> 00:07:43,230
Let's all go tonight.

96
00:07:43,230 --> 00:07:45,730
Um, what is this?

97
00:07:46,950 --> 00:07:48,610
I said it's your lunch.

98
00:07:48,610 --> 00:07:49,570
What?

99
00:07:50,450 --> 00:07:53,450
Th-This is all?

100
00:07:53,450 --> 00:07:56,960
What? You got a problem with that, huh?

101
00:07:56,960 --> 00:07:59,460
Not a problem, exactly...

102
00:08:00,130 --> 00:08:02,490
This is for both of us?

103
00:08:04,850 --> 00:08:06,190
You heard him.

104
00:08:06,190 --> 00:08:07,930
Good grief.

105
00:08:07,930 --> 00:08:11,290
Is this your first time being a slave?

106
00:08:11,290 --> 00:08:14,060
What? Well, yes.

107
00:08:14,390 --> 00:08:16,470
Then remember this.

108
00:08:16,470 --> 00:08:18,440
You're lucky you're getting fed at all.

109
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:22,610
Not only that, but us free men came
all the way here to bring you lunch.

110
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:26,070
You should start by thanking us.

111
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:29,970
These jerks...

112
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:32,820
Go on, say it.

113
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:36,080
Say, "Thank you."

114
00:08:39,330 --> 00:08:43,250
Why are you looking at me like that, asshole?

115
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:50,100
We'll take it. Thank you.

116
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:01,730
Thorfinn, you'd better
teach him some manners.

117
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:05,800
And don't injure the horse.

118
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:07,450
Yes, sir.

119
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:19,750
Those assholes are napping.

120
00:09:20,340 --> 00:09:23,720
They just came here to shirk their duties.

121
00:09:24,850 --> 00:09:29,770
And you shouldn't be so obedient
just because you're a slave.

122
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:34,850
Einar, push from the back.

123
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:36,740
I'll pull from the front.

124
00:09:40,990 --> 00:09:43,600
Once we get it to the river,
we'll use it to build a raft.

125
00:09:44,450 --> 00:09:48,040
Shouldn't we cut this tree a little shorter?

126
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:50,740
That old horse won't be able
to drag it by itself.

127
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:52,900
The trees belong to our master.

128
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:55,350
We can't cut them shorter
without his permission.

129
00:09:56,430 --> 00:10:00,430
Hey, isn't this their job?

130
00:10:00,430 --> 00:10:03,080
Normally you wouldn't let
a slave use a horse.

131
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:06,060
And this miserable horse alone
won't be enough.

132
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:07,590
Don't worry about it. Let's go.

133
00:10:18,100 --> 00:10:19,160
Einar.

134
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:20,350
O-Okay!

135
00:10:30,910 --> 00:10:33,240
Einar, lift the front.

136
00:10:34,030 --> 00:10:35,220
Got it.

137
00:10:45,110 --> 00:10:46,050
Let's go.

138
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:12,870
I'm so hungry, I feel sick.

139
00:11:14,790 --> 00:11:18,290
They won't get away with this.

140
00:11:18,730 --> 00:11:20,890
They ate my lunch.

141
00:11:22,270 --> 00:11:29,130
Retainers don't have their own farms,
so they have to serve a master, right?

142
00:11:29,630 --> 00:11:30,880
Yeah.

143
00:11:32,550 --> 00:11:37,400
Then they're halfway
to being slaves themselves.

144
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:41,890
They're just making sure there's
someone beneath them by bullying us.

145
00:11:45,470 --> 00:11:48,270
Don't you agree, Thorfinn?

146
00:11:49,990 --> 00:11:54,310
I don't know. It doesn't matter.

147
00:11:57,190 --> 00:11:59,790
It does matter.

148
00:11:59,790 --> 00:12:02,590
We're our master's property.

149
00:12:02,590 --> 00:12:06,120
His retainers can't push us around.

150
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:08,020
I'm going to tell our master about this.

151
00:12:08,930 --> 00:12:12,810
Don't. They'll just harass us more.

152
00:12:15,910 --> 00:12:19,110
And you're okay with that?

153
00:12:23,650 --> 00:12:25,890
Einar, Thorfinn...

154
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:28,100
Master.

155
00:12:29,390 --> 00:12:34,020
Well, Einar? How was your first day?

156
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:36,010
Actually, I have something to report.

157
00:12:36,010 --> 00:12:36,970
Don't.

158
00:12:36,970 --> 00:12:37,780
Shut up.

159
00:12:38,270 --> 00:12:41,050
I have something to report.

160
00:12:41,050 --> 00:12:45,020
Today, those retainers of yours...

161
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:05,320
What is it, Einar?
What do you have to report?

162
00:13:07,950 --> 00:13:09,830
What a strange fellow.

163
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:12,170
If you've got nothing to say,
then I'm leaving.

164
00:13:34,340 --> 00:13:35,240
Einar.

165
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:36,650
Huh?

166
00:13:37,910 --> 00:13:39,510
Weren't you going to report them?

167
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:46,580
Shut up.

168
00:14:09,190 --> 00:14:10,750
Hup.

169
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:17,430
It's hot today.

170
00:14:17,430 --> 00:14:19,090
We've got water.

171
00:14:20,380 --> 00:14:23,020
We just got it from the spring.

172
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:24,510
It's cold.

173
00:14:24,860 --> 00:14:26,680
Bring me a cup.

174
00:14:27,350 --> 00:14:29,000
High-speed turn!

175
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:34,010
Here you go.

176
00:14:34,010 --> 00:14:35,400
Thank you.

177
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:37,650
We went to the deep spring.

178
00:14:39,990 --> 00:14:42,780
I feel rejuvenated. Thank you.

179
00:14:43,760 --> 00:14:45,160
You're welcome.

180
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:47,870
Come on, everyone.

181
00:14:48,190 --> 00:14:50,220
We're almost done.

182
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:52,410
Let's finish this patch by noon.

183
00:14:52,410 --> 00:14:53,620
Yes, sir.

184
00:14:55,990 --> 00:14:58,790
The master's pitching in, too, huh?

185
00:14:58,790 --> 00:15:02,070
I thought rich people didn't work.

186
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:11,270
Danish or English, we all look
the same when we're working.

187
00:15:16,130 --> 00:15:18,480
Hey, not like that.

188
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:20,980
Don't make me say it again, Olmar.

189
00:15:20,980 --> 00:15:24,740
What? I'm just doing what you told me to do.

190
00:15:24,740 --> 00:15:26,490
Use a hand sickle.

191
00:15:26,490 --> 00:15:30,110
And cut it to below the knee.

192
00:15:30,110 --> 00:15:31,780
I showed you how to do this.

193
00:15:32,510 --> 00:15:35,030
Who cares as long as it gets cut?

194
00:15:35,030 --> 00:15:35,500
What?

195
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:38,920
You fool. After the harvest
comes the grazing.

196
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:43,630
We leave long stumps so
the livestock can eat them.

197
00:15:43,630 --> 00:15:48,520
You're 17, and you still haven't
learned the order of things.

198
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:52,280
That's why you don't understand
the purpose of each individual task.

199
00:15:53,030 --> 00:15:55,960
Shut up. I know.

200
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:57,890
I've got the order down pat.

201
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:01,750
Get this into that thick skull.

202
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:04,150
If you're going to lead others, then—

203
00:16:04,150 --> 00:16:06,440
Yeah, yeah. Below the knee, right?

204
00:16:06,870 --> 00:16:09,080
I got it.

205
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:09,990
Whoa!

206
00:16:09,990 --> 00:16:12,830
You fool! Don't swing your scythe like that.

207
00:16:12,830 --> 00:16:15,250
You'll crush the ears of the wheat.

208
00:16:15,250 --> 00:16:16,750
You said cut below the knee.

209
00:16:16,130 --> 00:16:19,690
What's going on over there?
He's getting an earful.

210
00:16:16,750 --> 00:16:17,670
I'm doing that.

211
00:16:17,670 --> 00:16:19,430
Do it properly.

212
00:16:19,690 --> 00:16:21,840
That's the master's son, Olmar.

213
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:23,050
Right there. Just like that.

214
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:24,130
Father and son, huh?

215
00:16:23,050 --> 00:16:24,130
Shut up.

216
00:16:25,030 --> 00:16:27,220
Ah, I can't take this!

217
00:16:27,810 --> 00:16:32,350
I thought I'd help out for once, and you
won't stop complaining about stupid shit.

218
00:16:32,350 --> 00:16:36,710
I'm out. I thought I'd help, but forget it.

219
00:16:36,710 --> 00:16:39,640
Hey, where are you going, Olmar?

220
00:16:39,980 --> 00:16:42,730
Somewhere you ain't, shithead.

221
00:16:42,730 --> 00:16:45,710
You'll be taking over this farm before long.

222
00:16:45,710 --> 00:16:47,530
You need to accept that.

223
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:51,690
When did I say I wanted
to take over this place?

224
00:16:51,690 --> 00:16:59,250
A grown man shouldn't be doing
this dull, boring, tedious farm work!

225
00:16:59,250 --> 00:17:01,330
I'm gonna use this to...

226
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:06,180
Huh?

227
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:12,010
What's he doing?

228
00:17:12,010 --> 00:17:12,540
What?

229
00:17:12,540 --> 00:17:13,770
I'm not sure.

230
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:28,210
I'm gonna make a name for myself
with a sword, damn it!

231
00:17:25,490 --> 00:17:28,870
Olmar! Wait, boy!

232
00:17:33,310 --> 00:17:37,580
I'm going to England soon.
I'll make sure of it.

233
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:44,040
I'm not spending my whole life here
in the middle of nowhere.

234
00:17:44,470 --> 00:17:49,490
I'm gonna join Prince Canute's army
and achieve greatness.

235
00:18:06,690 --> 00:18:11,320
Um... Sir, when is soon?

236
00:18:12,110 --> 00:18:14,200
Soon means soon.

237
00:18:14,490 --> 00:18:18,280
King Harald should be calling
for reinforcements soon.

238
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:23,460
I think you should take over the farm.

239
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:26,040
What? You, too?

240
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:27,630
What do you know?

241
00:18:27,630 --> 00:18:29,510
That's not what I meant.

242
00:18:29,510 --> 00:18:33,010
I'm just worried about you.

243
00:18:34,370 --> 00:18:36,680
Huh? Oh...

244
00:18:40,390 --> 00:18:41,270
Hey...

245
00:18:42,550 --> 00:18:45,300
Come here. Let's go again.

246
00:18:47,330 --> 00:18:51,290
Good, daughter of mine. That's it.

247
00:18:51,290 --> 00:18:52,680
How are things going?

248
00:18:53,310 --> 00:18:55,480
I brought food for the young master.

249
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:56,530
What?

250
00:18:57,700 --> 00:19:00,990
N-Not now. They're getting round two started.

251
00:19:00,990 --> 00:19:02,150
Oh, my!

252
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,750
Oh, my.

253
00:19:08,150 --> 00:19:11,470
With this, our family's future
will be secure.

254
00:19:11,470 --> 00:19:16,470
Exactly. As long as the young master
keeps coming here...

255
00:19:26,150 --> 00:19:28,440
Wh-Wh-Wh-What's the matter, sir?

256
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:30,690
Did our daughter commit some kind of blunder?

257
00:19:31,490 --> 00:19:33,610
Shut up, idiots!

258
00:19:33,610 --> 00:19:38,380
I know what you're up to,
you penniless tenant farmers.

259
00:19:38,380 --> 00:19:40,740
You're after my dad's fortune.

260
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:44,500
You think you'll get to live a life of
luxury if you join Ketil's family?

261
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:46,750
W-We'd never dream of that.

262
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,910
Women are rotten, every last one of them!

263
00:19:51,910 --> 00:19:55,760
Sir, that wasn't our intention!

264
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:58,010
Sir, wait!

265
00:19:58,930 --> 00:20:01,850
Damn it. What's wrong with everyone?

266
00:20:01,850 --> 00:20:04,890
I'm my own person, not my father's tagalong.

267
00:20:04,890 --> 00:20:07,930
Damn it! I feel like shit!

268
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:11,720
Hey, it's the young master.

269
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,930
Huh? The young master?

270
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:16,620
Hello, sir!

271
00:20:16,620 --> 00:20:18,030
Hey!

272
00:20:20,650 --> 00:20:22,990
What are you doing?

273
00:20:22,990 --> 00:20:25,180
It's dangerous to race around at night.

274
00:20:25,180 --> 00:20:26,660
So dangerous.

275
00:20:27,430 --> 00:20:29,670
What are you guys doing?

276
00:20:29,670 --> 00:20:34,280
We're coming over to you.

277
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:37,670
Come on. Walk straight.

278
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:44,570
We went to see a woman,
but the retainers beat us to her.

279
00:20:44,570 --> 00:20:46,520
Hey, the wheat...

280
00:20:44,570 --> 00:20:47,160
So we're drowning our sorrows.

281
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:53,070
But if we start a fight with them,
we'll get in trouble with our boss again.

282
00:20:53,070 --> 00:20:55,560
Screw that, right?

283
00:20:55,560 --> 00:20:58,190
Screw that.

284
00:20:58,190 --> 00:21:04,680
You're lucky. You can do
whatever you want on this farm.

285
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:08,580
Shut up. You guys don't know how I feel.

286
00:21:08,580 --> 00:21:11,050
What? Are you mad?

287
00:21:11,050 --> 00:21:12,870
You got something on your mind?

288
00:21:12,870 --> 00:21:15,480
Don't be mad.

289
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:19,340
I don't have time for you idiots.

290
00:21:19,790 --> 00:21:21,950
Go back to your fort and go to sleep.

291
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:26,510
Now, now, now, now, now, now...
Don't be so irritable.

292
00:21:26,510 --> 00:21:27,690
You're young.

293
00:21:27,100 --> 00:21:28,970
But you're so cold.

294
00:21:28,970 --> 00:21:31,480
H-Hey, don't try to lead my horse.

295
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:35,110
Don't worry about it.
Let's drink another round, okay?

296
00:21:35,420 --> 00:21:38,390
Let's stay up all night chatting, young master.

297
00:21:38,390 --> 00:21:40,610
Tell us all about your youthful troubles.

298
00:21:41,620 --> 00:21:44,950
You're hoping I'll entertain you
while you drink, aren't you?

299
00:21:44,950 --> 00:21:48,570
Screw this. I'm going home. Let go.

300
00:22:01,030 --> 00:22:04,010
He should just take over the farm.

301
00:22:04,740 --> 00:22:06,490
He doesn't know war.

302
00:22:07,710 --> 00:22:10,740
He probably thinks warriors are cool.

303
00:22:13,730 --> 00:22:17,540
Everyone who goes to war is a beast.

304
00:22:20,210 --> 00:22:23,150
Go to sleep. We have an early morning.

305
00:22:24,820 --> 00:22:30,100
Soldiers came to my village twice.

306
00:22:36,470 --> 00:22:41,090
First came the King of England's soldiers.
They burned down every single house.

307
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:46,340
My dad fought against them, but he was killed.

308
00:22:48,070 --> 00:22:51,480
All I could do was watch.

309
00:22:58,510 --> 00:23:02,550
After them came the Danes.

310
00:23:07,460 --> 00:23:10,820
They claimed they were saving us
from the tyranny of the King of England,

311
00:23:11,750 --> 00:23:14,450
but they pillaged everything they could.

312
00:23:21,890 --> 00:23:27,930
They're beasts wearing human skin.

313
00:23:33,430 --> 00:23:37,620
Hey, Thorfinn. Are you asleep?

314
00:25:36,850 --> 00:25:40,020
Snake

315
00:25:38,270 --> 00:25:39,320
"Snake."
